
* What is git revert, remove untracked files, What is tag, GitHub Clone?


{Git Revert}


* The revert command helps you undo an existing commit.
 

    * Reset  --->  Before Commit   (It means Git reset working before you commit, means Git reset remove changes from the staging area before committing)
    
    * Revert --->  After Commit    (It means Git revert working after you commit, means The revert command helps you undo an existing commit)


Commands-

- sudo su
- cd mumbai.git
- ls
- git status
- cat >newfile    ----> Create a new file and add some code in this file
- git add .
- git commit -m "code"
- git log --oneline
- git revert <commit-id>


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* How to remove Untracked files?


 - git clean -n     (Dry run)  (Ask to delete YES or NO)

 - git clean -f     (Forcefully)  (It doesn't ASK)


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

{Tags}


* Tag operatins allows giving meaningful names to a specific version in the Repository


Commands-


 - git tag -a <tag-name> -m <message> <commit-id>   (To apply Tag)

 - git tag    (To see the list of tags)

 - git how <tag-name>     (To see the particular commit content by using tag)

 - git tag -d <tag-name>  (To delete a tag)



---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


{GitHub Clone}


- Open GitHub website
- Login and choose existing Repo
- now, Go to your Linux machine and run command   ---->  git clone <URL of GitHub Repo>


# Its creates a local repo automatically in linux machine with the same name as in Github account



